WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:05.100
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video we'll be taking a deep dive into

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.960
the third season of Stranger Things, the easter
eggs you might have missed and the crucial

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:13.029
details from the ending and the post-credits
scene that set things up for season 4.

00:00:13.029 --> 00:00:17.620
Plus I'll explain exactly how the show tricked
you about Hopper in the finale.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.950
I've got a Stranger Things giveaway on this
video, so subscribe, hit the bell and let

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.140
me know what you thought of the new season
for a chance to win!

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:28.180
Obviously, spoilers ahead, so take care if
you're not all caught up.

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:32.700
Unlike Season 2 where Eleven closed the gate
and cut the Mind Flayer off from the Demodogs,

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:37.250
this time El has lost her powers for the moment,
so it's up to Joyce and Hopper to get to the

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:40.150
gate and destroy the machine that's keeping
it open.

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:44.940
As they try to turn the machine off, Hopper
is attacked by the Terminator-like Russian.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:48.970
Although Hop manages to push the goon into
the spinning machine, time is running out

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:54.280
to save the day, so he nods to Joyce signalling
that she has to shut the machine down herself

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:58.290
even though he's standing right next to it
which puts him in great danger.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:03.150
As the machine explodes, some nearby Russian
scientists disintegrate, the gate closes and

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:07.790
the connection between the Mind Flayer behind
the gate and its monster inside the mall is

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:09.640
broken, killing the beast.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:13.799
Now, if you're upset that Hopper was killed
in the explosion, there are plenty of clues

00:01:13.799 --> 00:01:15.560
to suggest that's not the case.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:20.180
First of all, after Joyce turned the keys
to shut down the machine, the screen conveniently

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:24.929
cut to black suggesting at least a few seconds
of time passed and that something happened

00:01:24.929 --> 00:01:26.450
off screen.

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:31.060
And as Joyce turns those keys, she looks down
and away from the platform presumably because

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:34.119
she can't bear to see what she thinks will
happen to Hopper.

00:01:34.119 --> 00:01:38.249
In reality though, it means that she wouldn't
have seen Hopper leave the platform.

00:01:38.249 --> 00:01:42.399
Because in the next shot, as we watch the
spinning machine go out of control and explode,

00:01:42.399 --> 00:01:46.570
if you look really closely at the platform
where Hopper was standing, you'll see there's

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:47.719
nobody there anymore.

00:01:47.719 --> 00:01:51.340
So, where did he go and why hasn't anyone
heard from him?

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:55.659
Well, there are a few possibilities including
one that the show hints at in the mid-credits

00:01:55.659 --> 00:01:57.399
scene at the end of the season.

00:01:57.399 --> 00:02:01.630
In this bonus scene, we discover that the
Russians are feeding human prisoners to a

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:02.630
Demogorgon.

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:07.169
But more crucially we find out that they've
got an American prisoner in one of their cells.

00:02:07.169 --> 00:02:11.420
If Hopper got off the platform before the
explosion and escaped into the nearby room

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:15.562
that Joyce and Murray run into later, it's
quite possible that he bumped into a group

00:02:15.562 --> 00:02:19.190
of Russians who apprehended him and hauled
him off to Russia.

00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:23.300
Another theory is that Hopper didn't have
time to find a safe exit before the machine

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:28.600
exploded and the gate closed, so rather than
stick around and risk being fried, he jumped

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:31.680
through the gate and is now stuck in the Upside
Down.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:32.930
"Three-inch minimum!

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:35.610
Leave the door open three inches!"

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:39.450
Perhaps that what the show is hinting at when
it shows Hop turn and look at the gate before

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:40.940
it closes.

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:44.340
And don't forget that Hopper has been in the
Upside-Down before when he went looking for

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:45.750
Will with Joyce.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:49.720
If he is now on the other side, there's no
immediate way out for him unless he can find

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:53.700
a breach back to our world, like El did at
the start of Season 2.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:58.570
A twist on this idea is that sometime after
Hopper jumped over to the other dimension,

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:02.710
the Russians figured out how to open up their
own connection to the Upside Down at their

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:07.190
base in Russia, and he emerges through there
which is how he's ended up in their cell.

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:11.290
An alternative theory is that the machine
the Russians developed has some similarities

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:15.740
to a particle accelerator, and that when it
blew up in Hawkins, it caused a rift in time

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:20.760
and space sending Hopper backwards in time
to the same location, for example, a year

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.850
ago, at which point he was captured by the
Russians.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:28.200
The final episode did have some heavy Back
To The Future references, so perhaps that's

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.150
what they were hinting at?

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:34.390
The other big clue that Hopper survived is
that the song "Heroes" plays while El is reading

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:36.630
Hop's "Heart to Heart" letter.

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:41.280
That same song played in the first season
when Will Byers' dead body was discovered,

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:46.510
and, as we all know, Will's death proved to
have been a fake and he's still clearly alive.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:50.880
And remember that, Hopper's adopted daughter,
El, also seemed to die at the end of season

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.960
1, disintegrating as she took out the Demogorgon.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.670
So, there's definitely hope for Hop!

00:03:55.670 --> 00:04:00.510
Now, although I'm convinced Hopper is still
alive somewhere, there are some alternative

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:04.230
possibilities for who the mysterious American
is inside the Russian cell.

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:09.440
Another character who's been heavily suggested
to still be alive is Dr Brenner, aka Eleven's

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:10.440
"Papa".

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:15.270
Although Brenner was mauled by the Demogorgon
in season 1, when El and her sister Kali visited

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:19.519
one of his ex-colleagues in the second season,
he claimed that Brenner was still alive:

00:04:19.519 --> 00:04:20.519
"Brenner!

00:04:20.519 --> 00:04:22.590
I can take you to him."

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:23.919
"Papa is gone."

00:04:23.919 --> 00:04:26.139
"No, he is alive."

00:04:26.139 --> 00:04:29.840
If Ray knew where Brenner was, it's quite
possible that the Russians tracked down the

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:33.999
former director of the Hawkins lab, to take
him captive and help them open a gate to the

00:04:33.999 --> 00:04:35.630
Upside Down.

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:39.409
Another possibility is that one of Eleven's
siblings from the Rainbow Room is locked in

00:04:39.409 --> 00:04:40.409
the cell.

00:04:40.409 --> 00:04:44.800
But it's also possible that the unnamed American
in the cell is an entirely new character being

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:47.159
introduced for Season 4.

00:04:47.159 --> 00:04:51.530
The other big revelation from the post-credits
scene is that the Russians are in control

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:52.940
of a Demogorgon.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:54.750
Which could mean a couple of things.

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:59.159
They may have discovered the Demogorgon during
their time in Hawkins, as we saw they had

00:04:59.159 --> 00:05:05.139
extra tall cages and electric cattle prods
which were presumably for containing the monsters.

00:05:05.139 --> 00:05:08.699
Or it might be proof that the Russians have
now managed to open their own gate to the

00:05:08.699 --> 00:05:13.240
Upside Down in Russia just as we saw them
trying to do in the opening scene of season

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.240
3.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:18.400
We can't discuss the finale of season 3, of
course, without talking about Billy and the

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:20.139
Mind Flayer's new monster.

00:05:20.139 --> 00:05:25.449
After the Mind Flayer was driven out of Will's
body in Season 2, the black particles weren't

00:05:25.449 --> 00:05:30.080
destroyed entirely and season 3 reveals that
they ended up at the abandoned steel works

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:32.139
building outside Hawkins.

00:05:32.139 --> 00:05:36.150
When the Russians open up the gate to the
Upside Down in their base below Starcourt

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:39.490
Mall, those black particles are reactivated.

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:44.870
In fact, Will's Stranger Sense or Will Tingle
is triggered when he feels the monster's presence

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:50.800
again after a swarm of nearby rats run past
him and into the Brimborn Steel Works building.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:55.280
The Mind Flayer now begins to slowly build
a new body for itself, starting with these

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:59.099
rats which burst open and combine to form
a new monster.

00:05:59.099 --> 00:06:03.479
The Mind Flayer then causes Billy to crash
his car, using the opportunity to possess

00:06:03.479 --> 00:06:08.589
him and use him not only as a human spy in
Hawkins, like the big bad did with Will in

00:06:08.589 --> 00:06:11.060
Season 2, but also to gather human victims.

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:13.300
"I want you to build."

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:14.639
"To build what?"

00:06:14.639 --> 00:06:16.120
"What you see."

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:20.839
The possessed Billy starts with his Lifeguard
colleague Heather and the pair then move on

00:06:20.839 --> 00:06:22.240
to her parents.

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:27.139
By the sixth episode, Billy has amassed around
30 people, who are now called "the Flayed"

00:06:27.139 --> 00:06:31.120
as they act like normal people until the Mind
Flayer activates them.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:35.159
At this point they all converge to the steel
works building where they melt down into a

00:06:35.159 --> 00:06:39.460
mess of bones and flesh and join the body
of the monster which grows bigger with each

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.520
new body it absorbs.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:47.009
And this is the meaning of the Latin title
of the episode "E Pluribus Unum" which translates

00:06:47.009 --> 00:06:52.119
as "Out of many, one", and fits with this
season's 4th of July Independence Day-setting

00:06:52.119 --> 00:06:55.819
as that phrase is also the original motto
of the United States.

00:06:55.819 --> 00:07:00.509
Before they join with the monster though,
the Flayed humans and rats will often consume

00:07:00.509 --> 00:07:03.619
toxic amounts of fertilizer and chemicals.

00:07:03.619 --> 00:07:07.900
It may be that the monster feeds off and grows
bigger from these chemicals, but the consumption

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:12.229
of these is also so that the human or animal
body is physically weakened and will easily

00:07:12.229 --> 00:07:13.979
melt and break down.

00:07:13.979 --> 00:07:17.940
Making this probably the grossest monster
on the show so far!

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:22.780
As the Mind Flayer's human spy for locating
Eleven, Billy is kept alive until the finale

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:26.539
where he's able to pin down El in the mall
after she loses her powers.

00:07:26.539 --> 00:07:31.800
Billy is about to offer Eleven to the monster,
but she helps him regain control of his mind

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:35.740
when she connects with him and reminds him
of his childhood with his mother.

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:40.039
Billy's self-sacrifice as he stands up to
the monster to stop it from getting to Eleven

00:07:40.039 --> 00:07:44.819
gives him a nice redemption arc and in this
case, unlike with Hopper, we did see his dead

00:07:44.819 --> 00:07:49.339
body, so I don't think he'll be coming back
to Hawkins, unless it's in flashbacks via

00:07:49.339 --> 00:07:51.999
Eleven or his stepsister Max.

00:07:51.999 --> 00:07:56.580
Cover-ups of what's really been going on in
Hawkins continue with the general population

00:07:56.580 --> 00:08:01.210
still seemingly unaware of the secret Russian
installation in the town or the fact that

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:05.110
it was the Mind Flayer's monster which was
responsible for destroying the Starcourt Mall

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:06.629
on the Fourth of July.

00:08:06.629 --> 00:08:11.509
The Cutting Edge exposé that runs on TV three
months later focuses blame for the mysterious

00:08:11.509 --> 00:08:16.150
goings-on and missing people on a corrupt
mayor and local government, chemical leaks,

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:20.199
and the programme even suggests that Satanism
may be at fault and links that to playing

00:08:20.199 --> 00:08:24.699
Dungeons and Dragons
"Some believe a rise in Satanism is to blame.

00:08:24.699 --> 00:08:29.440
To find out, tune in tonight at 8:00 p.m.
for 'Horror in the Heartland'"

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:33.750
Which is incredibly something some groups
have complained about in reality!

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:38.940
The TV documentary reminds me of how back
in Season 2, Murray told Nancy and Jonathan

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:42.940
that to reveal what had happened to Barb,
they needed to "water down" their story to

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:46.660
make it more palatable to the general public.

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:51.690
"Perhaps Barbara was exposed to some dangerous
toxins."

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:53.540
"A leak from the lab.

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:55.830
Like Three Mile Island or something."

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:58.080
"Something scary but familiar."

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:03.010
Interestingly enough, Season 3's secret Russian
invasion was partially predicted by Murray

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:05.490
himself right at the beginning of Season 2.

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:09.940
"I believe there was, and may still be, a
Russian spy presence in Hawkins."

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:10.940
"Russian spy?!"

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:14.340
"I'm talking a full-on Russian invasion right
here in Hawkins."

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:18.620
Murray might have been wrong about Eleven
being one of those Russians, but when Dr Owens

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:23.050
arrives at the end of season 3 and discovers
what's happened, he might be thinking back

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:27.880
to this conversation he had with Nancy and
Jonathan in season 2:

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:31.580
"Let's say, the Soviets...

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:35.270
If they heard about our mistake...
do you think they would even consider that

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:36.470
a mistake?

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:37.581
What if they tried to replicate that?"

00:09:37.581 --> 00:09:42.080
After all that happened in season 3, I wonder
if Season 4 will find Murray relocating as

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:45.960
he did say that Hopper and Joyce had compromised
his secure hideaway.

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:51.410
Since the end of Season 2 when the Mind Flayer
was shown watching over Hawkins School as

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:55.840
the ultra creepy song 'Every Breath You Take'
played, it's been hinted that the shadowy

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:58.120
monster has had his eye on Eleven.

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:03.390
And indeed she did turn out to be his ultimate
target this season, presumably in revenge

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:09.590
for her closing the gate in Season 2 and foiling
the Demogorgon in Season 1, and also because

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:14.250
it sees her as the main threat to its larger
plan for domination of our world.

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:19.380
After the monster bit Eleven and infected
her leg, it seems the Mind Flayer may have

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:23.101
at least temporarily weakened El, depowering
her for the final episode.

00:10:23.101 --> 00:10:28.460
This worked as a convenient plot device to
avoid a repeat of the season 2 finale where

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:33.160
Eleven did all the work of closing the gate,
but it also means that El can't search for

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:36.060
Hopper to confirm if he's really gone or not.

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:40.380
Mike is confident that Eleven's powers will
return and I expect this will be an important

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:42.930
part of her arc in Season 4.

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:47.510
The season ends with Joyce, Will and Jonathan
moving away from Hawkins taking Eleven with

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:48.510
them.

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:52.740
This splits up the gang, however, Mike mentions
meeting up around Thanksgiving and Christmas.

00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:58.030
I suspect that rather than Season 4 taking
place during the 1985 winter holidays, it'll

00:10:58.030 --> 00:11:02.810
be set around a year and a half after the
events of Season 3, putting it towards the

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:07.250
end of 1986, which will roughly keep it in
line with how the young actors are growing

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:08.850
up off screen.

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:13.430
And I wonder if Dustin will try and invite
his girlfriend Suzie for another rendition

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:18.140
of "The Neverending Story" or if she could
even travel from Utah to join them on their

00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:19.140
next adventure?

00:11:19.140 --> 00:11:23.900
Oh, and assuming Hopper does return next season,
I wonder if he'll be rocking his full-on Tom

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:25.590
Selleck as Magnum PI look again?

00:11:25.590 --> 00:11:28.850
"That's a lot of color for you, Chief."

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:29.850
It's cutting-edge!"

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:34.440
After all, I think Hop's love of Magnum isn't
just about what he calls the character's "cutting-edge"

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:38.500
look, but also about the fact that they're
both veterans of Vietnam.

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:44.440
One thing missing from Season 3 was any continuing
story about Kali who El met last season, but

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:49.100
if Dr Brenner does come back into play next
season we could see Kali or the other gifted

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.730
children from the Hawkins Lab appear.

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:55.870
You can learn more about them and the dark
history of Brenner's MK Ultra experiments

00:11:55.870 --> 00:11:58.980
in my Stranger Things Gifted Children video.

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:02.110
Tap the screen here or check the link in the
video description.

